# Optional. Most Gmail accounts should use an app password instead
# (Add account → Gmail). No client id, and no Google verification.
# Create one at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords after turning on
# 2-Step Verification. IMAP is imap.gmail.com:993 (TLS) and SMTP is
# smtp.gmail.com:465 (TLS) or 587 (STARTTLS). The username is the full
# email address. Some Workspace, school, and Advanced Protection accounts
# cannot create app passwords — use the tester sign-in below for those.
#
# "Sign in with Google (beta / testers)" needs a Desktop OAuth client.
# Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials.
# Enable the Gmail API. The Gmail scopes are restricted, so until Google
# verifies the app only test users on the OAuth consent screen can sign in.
# The button stays disabled when this is empty.
GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
# Optional — only if your client is a Web application type
# GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
